@Ιασων - This is not new. The capital-C Calorie has meant kilocalorie for longer than this old scientist has been  alive. I believe it goes back to the 19th century. 

I've done a fair amount of work in metabolic energetics, and our convention is to *always* use kilocalorie (not Calorie) where needed. But that is usually when referring to historic literature. In modern  usage, we use Joules or kiloJoules. 

Sadly, I believe dietitians etc. still use Calorie. They should modernize.

